{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833016884,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e462641f001G78kmErtDHXWp2","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e46245b90015Wgf31Qiv0xdRZ","type":"tool","id":"call_6f8d995e6ab74bc6a5317825","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"create:skill\" CONTRIBUTING.md README.md 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \"=== origin/main CONTRIBUTING names\"; git show origin/main:CONTRIBUTING.md | grep -o '/create:[a-z-]*' | sort | uniq -c"},"output":"CONTRIBUTING.md:155:Bug fixes with clear steps to reproduce them are the most welcome. Performance work with benchmarks and documentation fixes rank just as high. New skills, commands, agents and tests are welcome too. Scaffold a skill with `/create:sk-skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with several modes. Use `/create:command` and `/create:agent` for the others. Typo fixes, clearer code and English translations of non-English content are always welcome.\nREADME.md:269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\nREADME.md:603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== origin/main CONTRIBUTING names\n   1 /create:agent\n   1 /create:command\n   1 /create:skill\n   1 /create:skill-parent\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"CONTRIBUTING.md:155:Bug fixes with clear steps to reproduce them are the most welcome. Performance work with benchmarks and documentation fixes rank just as high. New skills, commands, agents and tests are welcome too. Scaffold a skill with `/create:sk-skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with several modes. Use `/create:command` and `/create:agent` for the others. Typo fixes, clearer code and English translations of non-English content are always welcome.\nREADME.md:269:Each kind also has a `/create` command for when you want the workflow directly. `/create:sk-skill` creates or updates a skill, and `/create:skill-parent` scaffolds a parent hub with its modes. `/create:agent` and `/create:command` cover agents and slash commands. `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:goal` and `/create:repo-rule` cover the documents around them. Every one runs with `:auto` or with `:confirm` to pause at each step.\nREADME.md:603:**Create (13).** `/create:sk-skill`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:agent`, `/create:command`, `/create:readme`, `/create:changelog`, `/create:feature-catalog`, `/create:manual-testing-playbook`, `/create:goal`, `/create:benchmark`, `/create:diff`, `/create:repo-rule` and `/create:with-human-voice`. These scaffold or revise one kind of artifact to the sk-doc standards.\n=== origin/main CONTRIBUTING names\n   1 /create:agent\n   1 /create:command\n   1 /create:skill\n   1 /create:skill-parent\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"create:skill\\\" CONTRIBUTING.md README.md 2>/dev/null | head -20; echo \\\"=== origin/main CONTRIBUTING names\\\"; git show origin/main:CONTRIBUTING.md | grep -o '/create:[a-z-]*' | sort | uniq -c\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833015839,"end":1794833016884}}}}
