{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833025215,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4628230001XcQyFAp8kNoGxd","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4626eba001kPApXdCboFzIdX","type":"tool","id":"call_b513ca1287e74854a21a2401","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/commands/doctor/ && echo \"=== CONTRIBUTING slash mentions with context\"; grep -n \"/doctor:\\|/create:\\|/speckit:\\|/deep:\\|/design:\" CONTRIBUTING.md"},"output":"_routes.yaml\nagents-md.md\nassets\nci.md\ndeep-loop.md\nenv.md\ngit.md\nhelper.md\ninstall.md\nmcp.md\noverlay.md\nruntime-mirrors.md\nscripts\nsetup.md\nsk-code.md\nsk-skill.md\nskill-advisor.md\nspeckit.md\nsymlink.md\nupdate.md\n=== CONTRIBUTING slash mentions with context\n36:The Spec Kit comes first, because the session hooks load its build and the advisor build uses its compiler. Open the clone in your runtime and run `/doctor:setup`. It checks the install without changing anything and names one repair command for each failing check. Run `/doctor:mcp install` only when your change touches Code Mode. The [install guide](INSTALL-SKILLED.md) has the full setup.\n155:Bug fixes with clear steps to reproduce them are the most welcome. Performance work with benchmarks and documentation fixes rank just as high. New skills, commands, agents and tests are welcome too. Scaffold a skill with `/create:sk-skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with several modes. Use `/create:command` and `/create:agent` for the others. Typo fixes, clearer code and English translations of non-English content are always welcome.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"_routes.yaml\nagents-md.md\nassets\nci.md\ndeep-loop.md\nenv.md\ngit.md\nhelper.md\ninstall.md\nmcp.md\noverlay.md\nruntime-mirrors.md\nscripts\nsetup.md\nsk-code.md\nsk-skill.md\nskill-advisor.md\nspeckit.md\nsymlink.md\nupdate.md\n=== CONTRIBUTING slash mentions with context\n36:The Spec Kit comes first, because the session hooks load its build and the advisor build uses its compiler. Open the clone in your runtime and run `/doctor:setup`. It checks the install without changing anything and names one repair command for each failing check. Run `/doctor:mcp install` only when your change touches Code Mode. The [install guide](INSTALL-SKILLED.md) has the full setup.\n155:Bug fixes with clear steps to reproduce them are the most welcome. Performance work with benchmarks and documentation fixes rank just as high. New skills, commands, agents and tests are welcome too. Scaffold a skill with `/create:sk-skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with several modes. Use `/create:command` and `/create:agent` for the others. Typo fixes, clearer code and English translations of non-English content are always welcome.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && ls .skilled/commands/doctor/ && echo \\\"=== CONTRIBUTING slash mentions with context\\\"; grep -n \\\"/doctor:\\\\|/create:\\\\|/speckit:\\\\|/deep:\\\\|/design:\\\" CONTRIBUTING.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833023536,"end":1794833025215}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833025227,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46285f80010j2IzY19JyofkS","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4626eba001kPApXdCboFzIdX","type":"tool","id":"call_680505554bf34fe3a67b36db","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,20p' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md; echo \"=== skill-parent\"; sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md"},"output":"---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nRoute /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n\n- Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n- Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n=== skill-parent\n---\ndescription: Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, registry source of truth). :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <mode1,mode2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:skill-parent Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:sk-skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nRoute /create:sk-skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n\n- Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n- Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n=== skill-parent\n---\ndescription: Scaffold a parent skill with nested mode packets (one hub identity, registry source of truth). :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [create|update] [--modes <mode1,mode2,...>] [--surfaces <s1,s2,...>] [--path <dir>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:skill-parent Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,20p' .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md; echo \\\"=== skill-parent\\\"; sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/create/skill-parent.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833024504,"end":1794833025227}}}}
