{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833165344,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e464a45b001ZBkBHpMmTafbQF","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4642436001tinE9acBqaw9ff","type":"tool","id":"call_e29818d920d14fb288b652df","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"/create:skill[^-]\" .skilled/commands .skilled/skills/sk-doc 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"sk-skill\" | head -20; echo \"=== assets\"; ls .skilled/commands/create/assets | head -20"},"output":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:43:  '| Skill | `/create:skill <name>` | Create a skill |',\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:85:    { command: '/create:skill', description: 'Create a skill' },\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:146:  const commandRows = without(COMMAND_ROWS, '`/create:skill <name>`');\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:149:  assert.match(out, /\\/create:skill not listed/);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:226:    { command: '/create:skill', description: 'Create a skill' },\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:28:- **`/create:skill` now blocks on the shape.** Its completion gate runs `validate_skill_package.py --strict`. So a routing-shape finding blocks creation. It does not print as a warning. The hub scaffold also keeps the compiled-routing directive in its final `## MACHINE ROUTER` section. That section is now numbered.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:30:- **New scaffolds start on the canon.** The skill and hub templates now emit it. So do the packet scaffold, the references and both `/create:skill` and `/create:skill-parent`. A fresh parent scaffold passes `parent-skill-check`. That is because `init_skill.py` renders `allowed-tools` as a list. Its `## MACHINE ROUTER` section keeps the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` the compiled router reads.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.6.0.md:3:description: \"package_skill.py --strict and parent-skill-check.cjs now fail a SKILL.md that has no MACHINE ROUTER section. The routing shape check gains a fifth code, and the canon docs and the /create:skill steps now list all five.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.6.0.md:24:- **The canon names all five codes.** The validation reference and the skill template now list every routing shape code. So do the `/create:skill` workflow steps. They also say a packet with no router block still ends with the section.\n=== assets\ncreate-agent-auto.yaml\ncreate-agent-confirm.yaml\ncreate-agent-presentation.txt\ncreate-benchmark-auto.yaml\ncreate-benchmark-confirm.yaml\ncreate-benchmark-presentation.txt\ncreate-changelog-auto.yaml\ncreate-changelog-confirm.yaml\ncreate-changelog-presentation.txt\ncreate-command-auto.yaml\ncreate-command-confirm.yaml\ncreate-command-presentation.txt\ncreate-diff-auto.yaml\ncreate-diff-confirm.yaml\ncreate-diff-presentation.txt\ncreate-feature-catalog-auto.yaml\ncreate-feature-catalog-confirm.yaml\ncreate-feature-catalog-presentation.txt\ncreate-goal-auto.yaml\ncreate-goal-confirm.yaml\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:43:  '| Skill | `/create:skill <name>` | Create a skill |',\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:85:    { command: '/create:skill', description: 'Create a skill' },\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:146:  const commandRows = without(COMMAND_ROWS, '`/create:skill <name>`');\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:149:  assert.match(out, /\\/create:skill not listed/);\n.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/command-catalog-mirror-check.test.cjs:226:    { command: '/create:skill', description: 'Create a skill' },\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:28:- **`/create:skill` now blocks on the shape.** Its completion gate runs `validate_skill_package.py --strict`. So a routing-shape finding blocks creation. It does not print as a warning. The hub scaffold also keeps the compiled-routing directive in its final `## MACHINE ROUTER` section. That section is now numbered.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.6.0.0.md:30:- **New scaffolds start on the canon.** The skill and hub templates now emit it. So do the packet scaffold, the references and both `/create:skill` and `/create:skill-parent`. A fresh parent scaffold passes `parent-skill-check`. That is because `init_skill.py` renders `allowed-tools` as a list. Its `## MACHINE ROUTER` section keeps the `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST` the compiled router reads.\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.6.0.md:3:description: \"package_skill.py --strict and parent-skill-check.cjs now fail a SKILL.md that has no MACHINE ROUTER section. The routing shape check gains a fifth code, and the canon docs and the /create:skill steps now list all five.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/changelog/v1.7.6.0.md:24:- **The canon names all five codes.** The validation reference and the skill template now list every routing shape code. So do the `/create:skill` workflow steps. They also say a packet with no router block still ends with the section.\n=== assets\ncreate-agent-auto.yaml\ncreate-agent-confirm.yaml\ncreate-agent-presentation.txt\ncreate-benchmark-auto.yaml\ncreate-benchmark-confirm.yaml\ncreate-benchmark-presentation.txt\ncreate-changelog-auto.yaml\ncreate-changelog-confirm.yaml\ncreate-changelog-presentation.txt\ncreate-command-auto.yaml\ncreate-command-c