{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833201652,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4653732001tmeWwTVk7JlsJY","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e464b238001j0KC5IQP13N7aa","type":"tool","id":"call_4715d1b8fd8f467396916011","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git show 74d3744e641 --stat | head -40"},"output":"commit 74d3744e64164596fac74b0f82e33144b220a2e7\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 17:52:46 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): rename the create skill command and offer the doctor helper\n    \n    The command /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime, with\n    no alias. A command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its\n    folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, an open upstream\n    bug. With the new file name Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands,\n    up from 32. The mirror check drops its allowlist and fails on a command\n    file named skill.md in any capitalisation. The sk-doc hub moves to\n    2.10.0.0 with a changelog entry that calls out the break.\n    \n    A doctor prompt that says a tool does not show up or appear now counts\n    as a strong problem cue, so the brief names /doctor:helper beside the\n    skills. The idioms \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue.\n    \n    The Gate 2 direct call in AGENTS.md sends the request on stdin, so a\n    prompt never sits in the process table. Its manifest and the Cursor\n    rule carry the same line.\n    \n    Five commands gain intent phrases: four doctor routes and the spec\n    search. On the real embedder, plain holdout reach reads 5 of 44, up\n    from 3, with typed recall and false offers unchanged.\n    \n    A brief-cost run points each hook child's temp folder at its sandbox,\n    so it writes nothing into the shared health log.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 183 files, 1,758 passed. Doctor tests 1,189,\n    0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n    Commit-Id: 0013878\n\n .claude/agents/markdown.md                         |    6 +-\n .claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md                |    1 +\n .claude/commands/create/skill.md                   |    1 -\n .codex/SYNC.md                                     |    4 +-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"commit 74d3744e64164596fac74b0f82e33144b220a2e7\nAuthor: Michel Kerkmeester <82775228+MichelKerkmeester@users.noreply.github.com>\nDate:   Fri Nov 13 17:52:46 2026 +0100\n\n    feat(system-skill-advisor): rename the create skill command and offer the doctor helper\n    \n    The command /create:skill is now /create:sk-skill on every runtime, with\n    no alias. A command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its\n    folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, an open upstream\n    bug. With the new file name Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands,\n    up from 32. The mirror check drops its allowlist and fails on a command\n    file named skill.md in any capitalisation. The sk-doc hub moves to\n    2.10.0.0 with a changelog entry that calls out the break.\n    \n    A doctor prompt that says a tool does not show up or appear now counts\n    as a strong problem cue, so the brief names /doctor:helper beside the\n    skills. The idioms \"appear to\" and \"up-to-date\" stay out of the cue.\n    \n    The Gate 2 direct call in AGENTS.md sends the request on stdin, so a\n    prompt never sits in the process table. Its manifest and the Cursor\n    rule carry the same line.\n    \n    Five commands gain intent phrases: four doctor routes and the spec\n    search. On the real embedder, plain holdout reach reads 5 of 44, up\n    from 3, with typed recall and false offers unchanged.\n    \n    A brief-cost run points each hook child's temp folder at its sandbox,\n    so it writes nothing into the shared health log.\n    \n    Floors held: typed recall 24/44, false offers 0/35, scorer eval\n    [160,50,21,5]. Suite: 183 files, 1,758 passed. Doctor tests 1,189,\n    0 failed.\n    \n    Spec: system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n    Commit-Id: 0013878\n\n .claude/agents/markdown.md                         |    6 +-\n .claude/commands/create/sk-skill.md                |    1 +\n .claude/commands/create/skill.md                   |    1 -\n .codex/SYNC.md                                     |    4 +-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && git show 74d3744e641 --stat | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833200946,"end":1794833201652}}}}
