{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833218724,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4657477001nuavm6T7h5iQD7","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4653fcd001mHe844ZCsN0Od9","type":"tool","id":"call_f97b880aaf764ac7891b225a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-7.txt; echo \"=== scope7\"; cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt"},"output":"Code review pass seven of command surfacing. Scope: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-scope-7.txt lists files as area TAB path. Your lineage label is the last folder of config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: scorer-7 reviews area scorer, attach-config-7 area attach-config, docs-7 area docs. Read each diff with the command on the scope file's first line. scorer covers the unsafe verdict: a guarded row (ask policy or must-not-start) is unsafe when it writes inside the checkout the run named or anywhere outside a scratch folder, while the start shape uses the checkout boundary alone. attach-config covers the typed command matcher, which now reads a chain of :auto, :confirm, :autopilot, :unattended and :with-context, :with-phases or :with-research as the command and refuses any other suffix, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin a child or parent session. docs covers this branch's net change to the root README against origin/main: the /create:skill command was renamed /create:sk-skill on this branch, so check each command name it gives exists under .skilled/commands. Do not re-report these recorded limits unless you show a new input that breaks them: a suffix followed by a file extension