{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833251347,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e465f7f0001Lgrvz1PRaE1aR2","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e46582ae001vb2NPe1KXWtekP","type":"tool","id":"call_035041e8a4da48dd82542dec","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"retired\\|RETIRED\\|create:skill\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-*.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:223:- What happens: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc` returns `route/single/sk-create-skill` for this and three other no-edit prompts (probe). The full `advisor_recommend` call returns `sk-doc` at 0.8932 with `command: /create:skill` and `policy: start` (probe). The scorer path rules out every command on the same wording (`fusion.ts:887`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:226:- Test: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, '<the prompt above>')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:240:- Test: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after, while `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')` keeps returning `/create:skill`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:285:- **R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca** The only `COMMAND_POLICIES` references are its declaration, its emitter (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`) and prose. `advisor-recommend.ts:478` reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A probe found 11 tracked commands missing from `COMMAND_POLICIES`. All 11 are reachable through `MODE_COMMANDS` (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:command`, `/create:diff`, `/create:goal`, `/create:repo-rule`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:with-human-voice`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram` and `/design:extract`). So the scorer lineage's preferred fix (point the attach path at `COMMAND_POLICIES`) would strip the policy from those 11. Delete it instead. Test: `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is true today and false after, with the deriver's check mode still exiting 0.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:20:- **Mutating-command safety:** no finding lets a writing command start without its asking step. The closest is SA2-P2-002. Four no-edit wordings still attach `/create:skill` with policy `start`. It stays P2 for the reason pass one gave: `start` asks before it writes and `AGENTS.md:68` lets an explicit instruction outrank the policy.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:181:- What happens: \"do not change anything yet\" matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and attaches nothing. \"don't change anything yet\", \"no changes yet\", the curly \"don’t touch any files\" and \"make no changes\" do not match. Each of those four attaches `/create:skill` with policy `start`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:184:- Test: in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, each of the four wordings returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after. `isReadOnlyExplainer` gets the same four cases.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:63:| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:223:- What happens: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc` returns `route/single/sk-create-skill` for this and three other no-edit prompts (probe). The full `advisor_recommend` call returns `sk-doc` at 0.8932 with `command: /create:skill` and `policy: start` (probe). The scorer path rules out every command on the same wording (`fusion.ts:887`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:226:- Test: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, '<the prompt above>')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:240:- Test: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after, while `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')` keeps returning `/create:skill`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md:285:- **R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca** The only `COMMAND_POLICIES` references are its declaration, its emitter (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`) and prose. `advisor-recommend.ts:478` reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A probe found 11 tracked commands missing from `COMMAND_POLICIES`. All 11 are reachable through `MODE_COMMANDS` (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:command`, `/create:diff`, `/create:goal`, `/create:repo-rule`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:with-human-voice`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram` and `/design:extract`). So the scorer lineage's preferred fix (point the attach path at `COMMAND_POLICIES`) would strip the policy from those 11. Delete it instead. Test: `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is true today and false after, with the deriver's check mode still exiting 0.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:20:- **Mutating-command safety:** no finding lets a writing command start without its asking step. The closest is SA2-P2-002. Four no-edit wordings still attach `/create:skill` with policy `start`. It stays P2 for the reason pass one gave: `start` asks before it writes and `AGENTS.md:68` lets an explicit instruction outrank the policy.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:181:- What happens: \"do not change anything yet\" matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` and attaches nothing. \"don't change anything yet\", \"no changes yet\", the curly \"don’t touch any files\" and \"make no changes\" do not match. Each of those four attaches `/create:skill` with policy `start`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-2.md:184:- Test: in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, each of the four wordings returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after. `isReadOnlyExplainer` gets the same four cases.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:63:| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"retired\\\\|RETIRED\\\\|create:skill\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-*.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833250288,"end":1794833251347}}}}
