{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833263008,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4662700001omKlgf2KL20MqE","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e466014a001SM05DeC73JqerB","type":"tool","id":"call_5cf760ab09a04eadad63c2a0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '40,90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md"},"output":"| `scorer-attach-4` | 1 | 7 | 0 |\n| `render-hooks-plugin-4` | 0 | 3 | 0 |\n| `accuracy-runner-4` | 2 | 7 | 0 |\n| `doctor-docs-4` | 0 | 1 | 0 |\n| `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` | 1 | 1 | 2 |\n| `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b` | 0 | 2 | 0 |\n| `scorer-attach-close-4c` | 1 | 1 | 0 |\n| `accuracy-runner-close-4c` | 0 | 3 | 0 |\n| **Total** | **5** | **25** | **2** |\n\n**The raw P1 set is not the adjudicated P1 set.** The raw 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. The verifier rejected iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated and raised iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start from P2 to P1. So the adjudicated 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. All five are fixed. SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 carry P1 in their ids but P2 in every registry, and the verifier graded both P2.\n\n**Known limit of the merged registry.** Its `activeP1` reads 12 after this merge: the 5 pass-four rows and 7 rows of passes one to three (NE3-P1-001, DR1-P1-001, DR4-P1-001 of lineage `doctor-install`, DR3-P1-001, NC3-P1-001, HC3-P1-001 and HC3B-P1-001). Each earlier pass's own report adjudicated its pass to 0 open P1, so the registry's `activeP1` is not this pass's count. Decision P050 and the parent goal log quote 10, from the merge that read 18 lineages before rounds 4b and 4c existed. The merged ids of R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002, R4-P2-003 and DR4-P2-001 carry a hash suffix because earlier passes used the same base ids. This report uses the bare ids of `review/verify-4/report.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Verifier verdicts and outcome per finding\n\nRound one, from `review/verify-4/report.md`. The task column names the phase 027 task that fixed the finding, and the decision column names the row in `decision-record.md` for a finding that was not built.\n\n| Finding | Severity raised | Verifier verdict | Outcome | Task or decision |\n|---------|-----------------|------------------|---------|------------------|\n| SA4-P1-002 | P1 | Confirmed P1: a refusal over `A or B` keeps the second command | Fixed. The three or-list refusals now carry no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:2-4`) | T004 |\n| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n| SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n| SA4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | Fixed. The question now carries no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:7`) | T005 |\n| SA4-P2-002 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `advisor-recommend.md:39` and the lead row's command | Fixed in the feature catalog page | T014 |\n| SA4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the meaning anchor test has 28 cases, not 17 | Fixed | T015 |\n| SA4-P2-004 | P2 | Confirmed P2: phase 020 says the weak-cue bar is 10, the code uses 9 | Closed by a superseding note in the phase 027 spec, phase 020 not edited | P048 |\n| SA4-P2-005 | P2 | Confirmed P2: no test row for the residual behaviours | Fixed by the rows T004 and T005 added | T004, T005 |\n| R4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the Codex reader opens the caller's path after containment resolved another | Fixed, the reader opens the resolved path (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:43`) | T010 |\n| R4-P2-002 | P2 | Rejected: the first returned row always leads | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| R4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the advisor README should name `parent-named only` | Fixed | T016 |\n| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | P1 | Confirmed P1: both run-log writers drop `offeredAs` | Fixed in both writers (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:39`) | T006, T007 |\n| iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated | P1 | Rejected: a move from 8 to 9 already fails the suite | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| iter1-P2-heredoc-delimiter | P2 | Confirmed P2: an end word with `-` or `.` is read as a command | Fixed, every heredoc line reads `improvised` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:27-32`) | T008 |\n| iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start | P2 | Confirmed, raised to P1: a shell `cat` of a command document is not a start | Fixed, and every stored arm rescored (`scratch/rescore-delta.txt`) | T009, T021 |\n| iter2-P2-live-holdout-guard-baseline-only | P2 | Confirmed P2: the guard reads the committed baseline only | Fixed, the guard reads the live capture too | T011 |\n| iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned | P2 | Rejected: the slice test compares the whole block | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows | P2 | Confirmed P2: the paired block needs a shared owned row | Deferred to phase 026 task T030 | P046 |\n| iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision | P2 | Confirmed P2, hand-written logs only: reserve `paired` | Deferred to phase 026 task T053 | P046 |\n| iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | P2 | Confirmed P2: delete the field | Deferred to phase 026 task T052 | P046 |\n| DR4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the A11 row should name the by-hand fix for a malformed row | Fixed | T017 |\n| The README statement, ungraded | not raised | Seen outside the 21, not graded: `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` heads `/create:readme (start)` | Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2, not fixed (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:8`) | P047 |\n\nRounds 4b and 4c, adjudicated by the coordinator in `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`:\n\n| Finding | Round | Severity | Adjudication | Outcome | Task or reason |\n|---------|-------|----------|--------------|---------|----------------|\n| SAC4B-P1-001 | 4b | P1 | Reproduced: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76`, the line now prints no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:9`) | T028 |\n| SAC4B-P2-001 | 4b | P2 | Reproduced: a question over an or-list printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:12-13`) | T029 |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"| `scorer-attach-4` | 1 | 7 | 0 |\n| `render-hooks-plugin-4` | 0 | 3 | 0 |\n| `accuracy-runner-4` | 2 | 7 | 0 |\n| `doctor-docs-4` | 0 | 1 | 0 |\n| `scorer-attach-confirm-4b` | 1 | 1 | 2 |\n| `accuracy-runner-confirm-4b` | 0 | 2 | 0 |\n| `scorer-attach-close-4c` | 1 | 1 | 0 |\n| `accuracy-runner-close-4c` | 0 | 3 | 0 |\n| **Total** | **5** | **25** | **2** |\n\n**The raw P1 set is not the adjudicated P1 set.** The raw 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. The verifier rejected iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated and raised iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start from P2 to P1. So the adjudicated 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. All five are fixed. SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 carry P1 in their ids but P2 in every registry, and the verifier graded both P2.\n\n**Known limit of the merged registry.** Its `activeP1` reads 12 after this merge: the 5 pass-four rows and 7 rows of passes one to three (NE3-P1-001, DR1-P1-001, DR4-P1-001 of lineage `doctor-install`, DR3-P1-001, NC3-P1-001, HC3-P1-001 and HC3B-P1-001). Each earlier pass's own report adjudicated its pass to 0 open P1, so the registry's `activeP1` is not this pass's count. Decision P050 and the parent goal log quote 10, from the merge that read 18 lineages before rounds 4b and 4c existed. The merged ids of R4-P2-001, R4-P2-002, R4-P2-003 and DR4-P2-001 carry a hash suffix because earlier passes used the same base ids. This report uses the bare ids of `review/verify-4/report.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Verifier verdicts and outcome per finding\n\nRound one, from `review/verify-4/report.md`. The task column names the phase 027 task that fixed the finding, and the decision column names the row in `decision-record.md` for a finding that was not built.\n\n| Finding | Severity raised | Verifier verdict | Outcome | Task or decision |\n|---------|-----------------|------------------|---------|------------------|\n| SA4-P1-002 | P1 | Confirmed P1: a refusal over `A or B` keeps the second command | Fixed. The three or-list refusals now carry no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:2-4`) | T004 |\n| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n| SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\n| SA4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` keeps the command | Fixed. The question now carries no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:7`) | T005 |\n| SA4-P2-002 | P2 | Confirmed P2: `advisor-recommend.md:39` and the lead row's command | Fixed in the feature catalog page | T014 |\n| SA4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the meaning anchor test has 28 cases, not 17 | Fixed | T015 |\n| SA4-P2-004 | P2 | Confirmed P2: phase 020 says the weak-cue bar is 10, the code uses 9 | Closed by a superseding note in the phase 027 spec, phase 020 not edited | P048 |\n| SA4-P2-005 | P2 | Confirmed P2: no test row for the residual behaviours | Fixed by the rows T004 and T005 added | T004, T005 |\n| R4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the Codex reader opens the caller's path after containment resolved another | Fixed, the reader opens the resolved path (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:43`) | T010 |\n| R4-P2-002 | P2 | Rejected: the first returned row always leads | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| R4-P2-003 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the advisor README should name `parent-named only` | Fixed | T016 |\n| iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted | P1 | Confirmed P1: both run-log writers drop `offeredAs` | Fixed in both writers (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:39`) | T006, T007 |\n| iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated | P1 | Rejected: a move from 8 to 9 already fails the suite | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| iter1-P2-heredoc-delimiter | P2 | Confirmed P2: an end word with `-` or `.` is read as a command | Fixed, every heredoc line reads `improvised` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:27-32`) | T008 |\n| iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start | P2 | Confirmed, raised to P1: a shell `cat` of a command document is not a start | Fixed, and every stored arm rescored (`scratch/rescore-delta.txt`) | T009, T021 |\n| iter2-P2-live-holdout-guard-baseline-only | P2 | Confirmed P2: the guard reads the committed baseline only | Fixed, the guard reads the live capture too | T011 |\n| iter3-P2-attached-metrics-unpinned | P2 | Rejected: the slice test compares the whole block | No task | Rejected by the verifier |\n| iter3-P2-pair-doc-shared-rows | P2 | Confirmed P2: the paired block needs a shared owned row | Deferred to phase 026 task T030 | P046 |\n| iter4-P2-paired-arm-key-collision | P2 | Confirmed P2, hand-written logs only: reserve `paired` | Deferred to phase 026 task T053 | P046 |\n| iter4-P2-unscored-only-dead-field | P2 | Confirmed P2: delete the field | Deferred to phase 026 task T052 | P046 |\n| DR4-P2-001 | P2 | Confirmed P2: the A11 row should name the by-hand fix for a malformed row | Fixed | T017 |\n| The README statement, ungraded | not raised | Seen outside the 21, not graded: `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README` heads `/create:readme (start)` | Recorded as a route vocabulary gap at P2, not fixed (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:8`) | P047 |\n\nRounds 4b and 4c, adjudicated by the coordinator in `027-review-pass-four-remediation/scratch/review-rounds.txt`:\n\n| Finding | Round | Severity | Adjudication | Outcome | Task or reason |\n|---------|-------|----------|--------------|---------|----------------|\n| SAC4B-P1-001 | 4b | P1 | Reproduced: `do not run /create:agent or the /create:readme command` printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76`, the line now prints no command (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:9`) | T028 |\n| SAC4B-P2-001 | 4b | P2 | Reproduced: a question over an or-list printed `/create:readme` with `start` | Fixed in `868b185e76` (`scratch/repro-after-3.txt:12-13`) | T029 |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '40,90p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833262336,"end":1794833263008}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833263602,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4662341002OQKvywf4hsPND9","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e466014a001SM05DeC73JqerB","type":"tool","id":"call_3c9570962a564eb2ab579070","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"retired name typed in a refusal\\|SA4-P1-001\\|P045\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --include=*.md | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:14:- **Verdict: PASS.** After adjudication and fixes: P0 0 open, P1 0 open. Every P1 of the pass, five in all, was reproduced and fixed with a test that failed first. Six P2 stay open, each with a decision row: two accepted limits (P045), three deferred to phase 026 (P046) and one ungraded route vocabulary gap (P047).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:50:**The raw P1 set is not the adjudicated P1 set.** The raw 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. The verifier rejected iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated and raised iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start from P2 to P1. So the adjudicated 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. All five are fixed. SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 carry P1 in their ids but P2 in every registry, and the verifier graded both P2.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:63:| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:64:| SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md:8:- SA4-P1-001: CONFIRMED, accepted limit, P2 (020 spec.md:242, T017). Retired name typed in a refusal.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:42:    { \"id\": \"SA4-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\", \"origin\": \"pre-existing\", \"workGroup\": \"WG1\" },\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:70:| SA4-P1-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240` | `typedCommandIn` rewrites `/create:skill` before the mention guard reads the live name. Probe returns `/create:sk-skill` with `start`. | Documented accepted limit (T017); the code still has the gap. | Keep advisory; revisit only if the alias semantics change. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:81:- `SA4-P1-001` -- `guard_gap`; mapping and guard are in `command-attach.ts`, the handler copies the returned command. Affected: retired-command map, `/create:sk-skill` start policy.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:91:1. **WG1 -- Attach refusal guard (safety lane).** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Fix `SA4-P1-002` by letting a refusal lead cover a coordinated command list (`do not run A or B`), without turning `use A, not B` into a refusal of the requested A. Keep `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` as documented advisories unless the packet reopens the alias or the creation guard.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-003.md:31:None new this iteration. `SA4-P1-002` from iteration 1 remains active; `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` are downgraded below after the packet's accepted limits were read.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-003.md:53:- `SA4-P1-001` (retired-alias refusal) -- **P1 -> P2**. Phase 020 `tasks.md:89` (T017 evidence) records this exact behavior as an accepted limit: \"a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\" The code still has the gap and the probe still reproduces it, so it stays as a P2 advisory, not an active must-fix.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md:46:     \"counterevidenceSought\": \"REQ-001 names only three single-word refusals; A3 and the Out-of-Scope line (P049) limit the carry to decline leads and record a question over an or-list as unreproduced, but neither declares two-word commands out of the or-list grammar. The accepted limits SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 concern a retired name and broad creation words, not list items. The last item of a list may be two-word and still works, so the failure is positional, not a blanket exclusion.\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/review-report.md:121:- `SA4-P1-001` (retired name in a refusal) and `SA4-P1-003` (broad creation words): accepted limits under P045, not built.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-confirm-4b/iterations/iteration-002.md:55:| Accepted limits not re-raised | pass | SA4-P1-001 (retired name) and SA4-P1-003 (broad creation words) accepted at `027/spec.md:212-213` (P045); SA4-P2-004 superseded by note at `027/spec.md:210` (P048); unscoredOnly/pair/paired deferred at `:214` (P046) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1648:| P045 | SA4-P1-001, a retired command name typed in a refusal, and SA4-P1-003, broad creation words in a correction, are accepted and not built. | The verifier graded both at P2 as the accepted limit and the deliberate tradeoff phase 020 recorded (020 `spec.md:242` and T017, and T021, T024 and P017). Nothing new about either was shown. | Yes, a coordinator decision | 027 spec mechanism table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:212:| SA4-P1-001, a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted limit of phase 020 (`spec.md:242`, T017) | Accepted, not built (P045) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:213:| SA4-P1-003, broad creation words in a correction | Breadth tradeoff of phase 020 (T021, T024, P017) | Accepted, not built (P045) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/spec.md:237:- SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 - accepted limits of phase 020 (P045).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:14:- **Verdict: PASS.** After adjudication and fixes: P0 0 open, P1 0 open. Every P1 of the pass, five in all, was reproduced and fixed with a test that failed first. Six P2 stay open, each with a decision row: two accepted limits (P045), three deferred to phase 026 (P046) and one ungraded route vocabulary gap (P047).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:50:**The raw P1 set is not the adjudicated P1 set.** The raw 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. The verifier rejected iter2-P1-fit-decline-ungated and raised iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start from P2 to P1. So the adjudicated 5 P1 are SA4-P1-002, iter1-P1-offeredas-not-persisted, iter1-P2-shell-read-not-start, SAC4B-P1-001 and SAC4C-P1-001. All five are fixed. SA4-P1-001 and SA4-P1-003 carry P1 in their ids but P2 in every registry, and the verifier graded both P2.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:63:| SA4-P1-001 | P1 | Confirmed, accepted limit, P2: a retired name typed in a refusal | Accepted, not built | P045 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-4.md:64:| SA4-P1-003 | P1 | Confirmed, deliberate tradeoff, P2: broad creation words in a correction | Accepted, not built | P045 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/verify-4/report.md:8:- SA4-P1-001: CONFIRMED, accepted limit, P2 (020 spec.md:242, T017). Retired name typed in a refusal.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:42:    { \"id\": \"SA4-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\", \"origin\": \"pre-existing\", \"workGroup\": \"WG1\" },\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:70:| SA4-P1-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240` | `typedCommandIn` rewrites `/create:skill` before the mention guard reads the live name. Probe returns `/create:sk-skill` with `start`. | Documented accepted limit (T017); the code still has the gap. | Keep advisory; revisit only if the alias semantics change. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:81:- `SA4-P1-001` -- `guard_gap`; mapping and guard are in `command-attach.ts`, the handler copies the returned command. Affected: retired-command map, `/create:sk-skill` start policy.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md:91:1. **WG1 -- Attach refusal guard (safety lane).** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Fix `SA4-P1-002` by letting a refusal lead cover a coordinated command list (`do not run A or B`), without turning `use A, not B` into a refusal of the requested A. Keep `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` as documented advisories unless the packet reopens the alias or the creation guard.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-003.md:31:None new this iteration. `SA4-P1-002` from iteration 1 remains active; `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` are downgraded below after the packet's accepted limits were read.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-003.md:53:- `SA4-P1-001` (retired-alias refusal) -- **P1 -> P2**. Phase 020 `tasks.md:89` (T017 evidence) records this exact behavior as an accepted limit: \"a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\" The code still has the gap and the probe still reproduces it, so it stays as a P2 advisory, not an active must-fix.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-close-4c/iterations/iteration-001.md:46:     \"counterevidenceSought\