{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833341816,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4675685001zq93eiX0eiE85m","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4668b2b001W1c2YnGTxQ1rLq","type":"tool","id":"call_094606fa9f404806bcdd7707","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md; echo \"=== commands README\"; sed -n '1,40p' .skilled/commands/create/README.txt"},"output":"---\ndescription: \"Install or debug Code Mode, its UTCP configuration, and runtime registration.\"\nargument-hint: \"<install [--runtime <name>]|debug [--fix]>\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:mcp Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It resolves the MCP sub-action and setup values, then loads the matching workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n=== commands README\n---\ntitle: \"Create Commands\"\ndescription: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"create command\"\n  - \"scaffold component\"\n  - \"create agent\"\n  - \"create skill\"\n  - \"create readme\"\n  - \"create feature catalog\"\n  - \"create testing playbook\"\n  - \"create changelog\"\n  - \"create chart\"\n  - \"create diagram\"\n  - \"create diff\"\n  - \"create repo rule\"\n  - \"apply human voice\"\n---\n\n# Create Commands\n\n> Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n\nThe table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n\nAll shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n\nThis document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: \"Install or debug Code Mode, its UTCP configuration, and runtime registration.\"\nargument-hint: \"<install [--runtime <name>]|debug [--fix]>\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:mcp Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It resolves the MCP sub-action and setup values, then loads the matching workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n=== commands README\n---\ntitle: \"Create Commands\"\ndescription: \"Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, docs, changelogs, charts, diagrams, diffs and repo rules.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"create command\"\n  - \"scaffold component\"\n  - \"create agent\"\n  - \"create skill\"\n  - \"create readme\"\n  - \"create feature catalog\"\n  - \"create testing playbook\"\n  - \"create changelog\"\n  - \"create chart\"\n  - \"create diagram\"\n  - \"create diff\"\n  - \"create repo rule\"\n  - \"apply human voice\"\n---\n\n# Create Commands\n\n> Slash commands for scaffolding OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, charts, diagrams, diff reports and repo rules with proper templates and validation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThe `create` command group scaffolds OpenCode components, documentation packages, changelog entries, and standalone visual and prose artifacts. All commands follow a structured YAML workflow and support `:auto` (no approval prompts) and `:confirm` (pause at each step) execution modes.\n\nThe table in section 3 lists every command in this folder. When a command file is added here, add its row there too; a missing row is the failure mode this index has hit before.\n\nAll shipped `create` commands run Phase 0 (@markdown agent self-verification).\n\n---\n\n## 2. PURPOSE\n\nUse this index to understand which `/create:*` command owns a given scaffolding workflow, which argument shape it expects, and which package contract or artifact family it generates.\n\nThis document is a routing and reference surface only. Run the command entrypoint itself for execution, setup prompting, and YAML workflow dispatch.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/mcp.md; echo \\\"=== commands README\\\"; sed -n '1,40p' .skilled/commands/create/README.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833340037,"end":1794833341816}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833341824,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46759bd001nLTTmfnbRWHtok","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4668b2b001W1c2YnGTxQ1rLq","type":"tool","id":"call_81f03eeca9a64ee19a2773b9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md; echo \"=== create command\"; sed -n '1,8p' .skilled/commands/create/command.md; echo \"=== create agent\"; sed -n '1,8p' .skilled/commands/create/agent.md"},"output":"---\ndescription: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\nargument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:setup Router\n\nThis command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n=== create command\n---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode slash command sets with :auto/:confirm workflow assets.\nargument-hint: \"<command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:command Router\n\n=== create agent\n---\ndescription: Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto|:confirm] (:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: prompt-body block for non-interactive setup)\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:agent Router\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: \"List every doctor target and run the read-only setup checks, naming the repair command for each failing leg.\"\nargument-hint: \"(no arguments)\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob\n---\n<!-- skill_agent: system-skilled-doctor -->\n\n# /doctor:setup Router\n\nThis command is a thin, read-only router. It lists every doctor command and target with what each checks, runs the existing read-only checks once, and prints the runnable repair command for each failing leg. It writes nothing in the repository.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n=== create command\n---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode slash command sets with :auto/:confirm workflow assets.\nargument-hint: \"<command_invocation> [command_request] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:command Router\n\n=== create agent\n---\ndescription: Create a new OpenCode agent with frontmatter, tool permissions, behavioral rules. Modes :auto, :confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<agent_name> [agent_description] [:auto|:confirm] (:auto supports PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS: prompt-body block for non-interactive setup)\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:agent Router\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '1,12p' .skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md; echo \\\"=== create command\\\"; sed -n '1,8p' .skilled/commands/create/command.md; echo \\\"=== create agent\\\"; sed -n '1,8p' .skilled/commands/create/agent.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833340861,"end":1794833341824}}}}
