{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833371980,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e467d046001AUbfXB7KbgEVMA","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4677ed4001ok61C6jFbY2S9t","type":"tool","id":"call_c117d4c54e34480693aefe7e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"retired\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:459:  it('reads a retired command name as the command that replaced it', () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:469:  it('does not read a retired name inside a path', () => {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:459:  it('reads a retired command name as the command that replaced it', () => {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:469:  it('does not read a retired name inside a path', () => {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"retired\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833371206,"end":1794833371980}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833371988,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e467cc8a001Fdb74DmfiVraEZ","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4677ed4001ok61C6jFbY2S9t","type":"tool","id":"call_80e4c65cbb014cfab1f5a219","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '230,250p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-*/spec.md 2>/dev/null; ls specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/ | head -30"},"output":"\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Every gate fails toward no offer: a prompt the gate misreads keeps its skill and loses only the command.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n## L2: EDGE CASES\n<!-- FILL: Name the empty input, the maximum input and the failure path. One line each. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Empty input: an empty `logs/archive/` deletes nothing and exits 0. Maximum: `--keep 3` over 10,000 archives keeps the newest 3. Failure path: a missing `--keep` value exits 2 with usage. WEAK: Handle edge cases. -->\n\n- Empty input: an empty prompt or a prompt that names no command returns `false` from `commandOnlyMentioned` and changes no row.\n- Maximum input: a prompt that names two commands is read once per command, so `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` keeps the first and withholds the second.\n- Failure path: a prompt that asks about a command and then asks for it with a pronoun (`what does /create:readme do? run it on the hooks folder`) loses the command and keeps `sk-doc`. A retired name such as `/create:skill` is not read as a mention of its successor and keeps today's behaviour.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n001-command-routing-baseline-corpus\n002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata\n003-plain-chat-command-reach\n004-command-meaning-matching\n005-recommendation-contract-and-brief\n006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost\n009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research\n010-reachability-and-attribution\n011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n012-plain-offer-reach\n013-attribution-and-install-reach\n014-review-remediation\n015-health-default-and-brief-refinements\n016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n017-review-pass-two-remediation\n018-holdout-row-retirement\n019-workflow-outcome-measure\n020-command-offer-fit-guards\n021-brief-head-parity\n022-workflow-measure-soundness\n023-untuned-outcome-evidence\n024-fable-review-remediation\n025-release-notes-and-doc-sync\n026-untuned-behaviour-arm\n027-review-pass-four-remediation\n028-direct-call-off-switch\n029-direct-call-kill-switch\n030-vibe-runtime-parity\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Every gate fails toward no offer: a prompt the gate misreads keeps its skill and loses only the command.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n## L2: EDGE CASES\n<!-- FILL: Name the empty input, the maximum input and the failure path. One line each. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Empty input: an empty `logs/archive/` deletes nothing and exits 0. Maximum: `--keep 3` over 10,000 archives keeps the newest 3. Failure path: a missing `--keep` value exits 2 with usage. WEAK: Handle edge cases. -->\n\n- Empty input: an empty prompt or a prompt that names no command returns `false` from `commandOnlyMentioned` and changes no row.\n- Maximum input: a prompt that names two commands is read once per command, so `use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete` keeps the first and withholds the second.\n- Failure path: a prompt that asks about a command and then asks for it with a pronoun (`what does /create:readme do? run it on the hooks folder`) loses the command and keeps `sk-doc`. A retired name such as `/create:skill` is not read as a mention of its successor and keeps today's behaviour.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:edge-cases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:complexity -->\n## L2: COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n<!-- FILL: Score each row with the number the change earns. The total must match the level. Write `N/A` with one reason, or delete the whole section. GOOD: Scope 6/25: one option in `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. Total 18/100. WEAK: Complexity is medium. -->\n\n001-command-routing-baseline-corpus\n002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata\n003-plain-chat-command-reach\n004-command-meaning-matching\n005-recommendation-contract-and-brief\n006-gate-2-binding-and-runtime-pointers\n007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof\n008-embedder-setup-and-cost\n009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research\n010-reachability-and-attribution\n011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n012-plain-offer-reach\n013-attribution-and-install-reach\n014-review-remediation\n015-health-default-and-brief-refinements\n016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n017-review-pass-two-remediation\n018-holdout-row-retirement\n019-workflow-outcome-measure\n020-command-offer-fit-guards\n021-brief-head-parity\n022-workflow-measure-soundness\n023-untuned-outcome-evidence\n024-fable-review-remediation\n025-release-notes-and-doc-sync\n026-untuned-behaviour-arm\n027-review-pass-four-remediation\n028-direct-call-off-switch\n029-direct-call-kill-switch\n030-vibe-runtime-parity\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '230,250p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfaci