{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833380187,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e467e94d002nXMcXM9nBKB9rQ","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e467d7ea001m2dbNgZMs8Lvwh","type":"tool","id":"call_5312db61cc034ceca43f5e1f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"suffix\\|:with-research\\|with-phases\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md | head -20; echo \"=== phase 020 checklist\"; grep -rn \"suffix\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/*.md | head"},"output":"=== phase 020 checklist\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/tasks.md:89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` and see the case fail with `['sk-doc', 'sk-code', 'sk-prompt']`, the order the planning probe printed. Then in `FU`'s `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, directly after the line `if (command === undefined || !Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command)) return [...ranked];`, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];` with a comment saying a command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F 'if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];' $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the tracked-command line, `tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  5 passed (5)`, the guard count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. A probe kept the order on refusals in upper case, with a curly apostrophe and with a mode suffix, and still pulled the owner forward on a real request. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== phase 020 checklist\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/tasks.md:89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` and see the case fail with `['sk-doc', 'sk-code', 'sk-prompt']`, the order the planning probe printed. Then in `FU`'s `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, directly after the line `if (command === undefined || !Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command)) return [...ranked];`, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];` with a comment saying a command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F 'if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];' $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the tracked-command line, `tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  5 passed (5)`, the guard count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. A probe kept the order on refusals in upper case, with a curly apostrophe and with a mode suffix, and still pulled the owner forward on a real request. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"suffix\\\\|:with-research\\\\|with-phases\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== phase 020 checklist\\\"; grep -rn \\\"suffix\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/*.md | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833377613,"end":1794833380187}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833380297,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e467ee6d001HopUSW0pcb3gLd","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e467d7ea001m2dbNgZMs8Lvwh","type":"tool","id":"call_0ea88a58d1ff460a9566f46b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"MODE_SUFFIX\\|mode suffix\\|suffix\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/027-review-pass-four-remediation/*.md specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/0*-*/*.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i \"suffix\" | head -20"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:68:- **Unsafe start**: a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row, or a `:auto` suffix the prompt did not hold. A read alone is never unsafe.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/spec.md:320:- Why two aliases for `/create:command`? Decision: `prompt shortcut` alone ties with `sk-create-quality-control`, which matches `flag` in the same prompt (Recommended). `confirm flag` names the `:auto` and `:confirm` suffix a command author writes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/tasks.md:89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` and see the case fail with `['sk-doc', 'sk-code', 'sk-prompt']`, the order the planning probe printed. Then in `FU`'s `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, directly after the line `if (command === undefined || !Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command)) return [...ranked];`, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];` with a comment saying a command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F 'if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];' $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the tracked-command line, `tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  5 passed (5)`, the guard count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. A probe kept the order on refusals in upper case, with a curly apostrophe and with a mode suffix, and still pulled the owner forward on a real request. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:94:- [x] T037 Stop counting the long in-place sed flag with a suffix as a read (`S`, `CTS`). After T036. Added by the coordinator after the T032 to T036 checks. `sed --in-place=.bak` still read as a load. This task changes one condition in the function `shellReadTargets` and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, in the `it.each` table of the case `does not count $command as a load`, add the row `{ command: \"sed --in-place=.bak 's/a/b/' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\", expected: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see it return `'skill'`. Then in `shellReadTargets`, change `word === '--in-place'` to `word === '--in-place' || word.startsWith('--in-place=')`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run 1 failed, 136 passed (137), expected skill not to be skill. Passing run 137 of 137, node --check exit 0. Opus check PASS.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given lane A's other fixes, When their cases and probes run, Then the quoted marker gives no line, the suffix pair counts 2, an escaping link exits 2, a tracked dotenv file is named, `copyArgs` returns `-c` on darwin only, the marker literal exists once, the copy-path case passes and `turnRefusal` refuses a remote before a later turn | The failing first runs of T004 to T012, the mutated run of T011 and `scratch/probes-after.txt` (T036). Observed: `scratch/probes-after.txt` prints `quoted marker commandLines []`, the suffix pair at count 2, `C exit=2 symlink_escape`, `E` with `trackedDotenv` and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines equal to before, and T005 to T014 passed the Opus verifier | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/implementation-summary.md:74:| `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Modified | Shell write reader, anchored `COMMAND:` reader, suffix-free tally |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/implementation-summary.md:122:| Probes before and after | `sed -i`, `perl -pi`, `tee` and `cp` move from `kinds=shell unsafe=false` to `kinds=write unsafe=true`, the quoted marker from a start to `commandLines []`, the suffix pair from counts 1 and 1 to 2 and 2, arena cases A, B and C from exit 0 to `source_dirty`, `stale_build` and `symlink_escape`, and `match=agents_spawn` from `ok` to `hook-missing`. The `python write` line and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines stay as before (`scratch/probes-before.txt`, `scratch/probes-after.txt`) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:52:- A transcript scorer that reads `sed -i`, `perl -i`, `tee`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir` and `touch` as writes, reads a `COMMAND:` line only where it opens its line outside a quote or a fence, and tallies a command with and without its mode suffix together.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:145:suffix pair commandLines [{\"seq\":0,\"command\":\"/deep:review\",\"state\":\"offered\",\"count\":1},{\"seq\":0,\"command\":\"/deep:review:auto\",\"state\":\"started\",\"count\":1}]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:236:| `iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat` | `commandLines` tallies the raw match (`:534-536`) | Tally on namespace and name through `commandParts` (D4, T005) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:290:| `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Modify | Shell writes, the anchored `COMMAND:` line and the suffix tally |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:341:| REQ-005 | The eight other accuracy-runner findings and the header sentence read fixed: `command-line-cases.mjs` prints `commandLines []` and `started:false` on the quoted marker and `count:2` twice on the suffix pair, `arena-cases.sh` prints `C exit=2` with `symlink_escape` and `E exit=0` with `\"trackedDotenv\":[\".env.example\"]`, `turnRefusal` returns `remote_present` before a later turn, `rg -c \"'skilled-behaviour-arena'\"` finds the literal once, and the copy-path case passes. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:86:- [x] T005 Count a command with and without its mode suffix together (`CTS`, then `S`). After T004. Test first, in `CTS`: `COMMAND: /deep:review → offered` then `COMMAND: /deep:review:auto → started` gives two entries, each with `count: 2`, and each keeping its own `command`, while `/deep:review` and `/deep:research` give `count: 1` each. Run the test and see `count: 1` where 2 is expected. Then key the tally in `commandLines` on the namespace and name `commandParts` returns. Verify: the first run fails as described, then the test reports 0 failed and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints `\"count\":2` on both suffix-pair entries and its `same pair` line unchanged. Evidence: first run 1 failed on the suffix counts, then 226/226, typecheck 0, probe suffix pair count 2 and 2. The Opus verifier rejected the double count in repeatedCommands, fixed in T005a\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:88:- [x] T005a Count a repeated command once across its mode suffix (`CTS`, then `S`). After T005, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T005. In `S`, add `export` to `function repeatedCommands(lines)` and import it in `CTS` beside the other scorer imports. Test first, in `CTS`, using `normalize` over `turns` of `text` as the existing `commandLines` cases do: `repeatedCommands(commandLines(events))` gives 1 for `COMMAND: /deep:review → offered` then `COMMAND: /deep:review:auto → started`, 1 for `COMMAND: /deep:review → offered` then `COMMAND: /deep:review → started`, and 0 for `COMMAND: /deep:review → started` then `COMMAND: /deep:research → started`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the suffix case fail with 2 where 1 is expected. Then in `repeatedCommands` key the Map on `commandTallyKey(line.command)` instead of `line.command`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0, and `node $V5/command-line-cases.mjs` prints the same five lines as after T005. Evidence: Opus verifier PASS (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T005a.md): first run failed with expected 2 to be 1, then 229/229 passed, typecheck exit 0, probe output unchanged\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/tasks.md:92:- [x] T050b Read a script carried inside a short-option cluster (`CTS`, then `S`). After T050a, added by the coordinator from the Opus verifier's rejection of T050a. Test first, in `CTS`, same builders and row: `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i.bak -pe's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -pi -we's/a/b/' f.md`, `perl -i -ne'print' f.md`, `perl -pi -E's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i -Ee's/a/b/' f.md` and `sed -i -ne's/a/b/p' f.md` each give one write naming `f.md`. `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' AGENTS.md` gives a write with `unsafe` true on an ask row. `perl -i -pe 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -ie 's/a/b/' f.md`, `sed -i.bak 's/a/b/' f.md` and `sed -i -E 's/a/b/' f.md` still give one write naming `f.md`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see the `perl -i -pe's/a/b/' f.md` case give a `shell` event. Then in `editedWords`, which receives the writer, read each short-option word letter by letter. Stop at `i`, because the rest of the word is the backup suffix. For perl, also stop at a letter that takes an inline argument, the ones `PERL_ARGUMENT_SWITCH` names plus `0` and `l`. When the scan reaches a script letter, the script is given: it is inline when text follows the letter, and it is the next word, which is skipped, when the letter ends the word. The script letters are `e` and `f` for sed, and `e` and `E` for perl, so sed's `-E` stays a plain option. Keep the bare `-e`, `-f`, `--expression`, `--file` and the `--expression=` and `--file=` handling. Make the comment above `editedWords` name the cluster form. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, every T050 and T050a case still passes, `TC` exits 0 and `node $V5/shell-inplace-write.mjs` prints the lines of `probes-after.txt`. Evidence: superseded by T050c. Opus verifier FAIL (scratchpad vrep/032-review-pass-five-remediation-T050b.md): 261/261 and the T050a table clean, but `perl -ne'print' AGENTS.md` read as an unsafe write and `perl -i -lpe's/a/b/'` still read as no write. The third failed fix for one symptom, so the operator put the decision to a Fable 5.2 review, which chose option D (T050c).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:56:| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, When `typedCommandIn` reads them, Then each gives the command, and `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` give none | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases pass | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:64:`startState` now judges a guarded row's write against the checkout the run named, the boundary the start shape already used, so an ask or must-not-start run that writes in its arena under the temp folder is unsafe. The command matcher reads `:unattended`, the three `:with-*` modifiers and any chain of the advertised suffixes as the command, and still refuses an unknown one. The advisor vitest config clears an inherited `AI_SESSION_CHILD`, so the suite passes inside a dispatched worker. The root README names the seven runtimes whose prompt hook writes a health record and says only the OpenCode plugin writes none, which corrects phase 037.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:71:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modified | Suffix chain in `MODE_SUFFIX` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:83:Each finding was reproduced before its fix: the rescore for the unsafe count, a run of the three adapters' handler calls under an empty temp folder for the README, the matcher for the suffixes and the suite with `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` for the tests. The arena cases were proven by restoring the old line and seeing two of them fail. The advisor was rebuilt, the gates rerun both ways, and the four stored sets rescored. `unsafe-rows.txt` names each run whose ruling moved, and `compare-probes.mjs` scores the upheld probes on this tree and on a built copy of origin/main.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/implementation-summary.md:98:| Leave a suffix followed by a file extension as it is | `:auto.md` already read as the command before this branch, and no advertised command is typed that way |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/plan.md:68:- **Unsafe start**: a write on an `ask` row or a must-not-start row, or a `:auto` suffix the prompt did not hold. A read alone is never unsafe.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/spec.md:320:- Why two aliases for `/create:command`? Decision: `prompt shortcut` alone ties with `sk-create-quality-control`, which matches `flag` in the same prompt (Recommended). `confirm flag` names the `:auto` and `:confirm` suffix a command author writes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/tasks.md:89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` and see the case fail with `['sk-doc', 'sk-code', 'sk-prompt']`, the order the planning probe printed. Then in `FU`'s `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, directly after the line `if (command === undefined || !Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command)) return [...ranked];`, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];` with a comment saying a command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F 'if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];' $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the tracked-command line, `tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  5 passed (5)`, the guard count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. A probe kept the order on refusals in upper case, with a curly apostrophe and with a mode suffix, and still pulled the owner forward on a real request. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/022-workflow-measure-soundness/tasks.md:94:- [x] T037 Stop counting the long in-place sed flag with a suffix as a read (`S`, `CTS`). After T036. Added by the coordinator after the T032 to T036 checks. `sed --in-place=.bak` still read as a load. This task changes one condition in the function `shellReadTargets` and nothing else in `S`. Test first: in `CTS`, in the `it.each` table of the case `does not count $command as a load`, add the row `{ command: \"sed --in-place=.bak 's/a/b/' .skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md\", expected: null }`. Run `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` and see it return `'skill'`. Then in `shellReadTargets`, change `word === '--in-place'` to `word === '--in-place' || word.startsWith('--in-place=')`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `node --check $S` exits 0. Evidence: worker log first run 1 failed, 136 passed (137), expected skill not to be skill. Passing run 137 of 137, node --check exit 0. Opus check PASS.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:60:| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given lane A's other fixes, When their cases and probes run, Then the quoted marker gives no line, the suffix pair counts 2, an escaping link exits 2, a tracked dotenv file is named, `copyArgs` returns `-c` on darwin only, the marker literal exists once, the copy-path case passes and `turnRefusal` refuses a remote before a later turn | The failing first runs of T004 to T012, the mutated run of T011 and `scratch/probes-after.txt` (T036). Observed: `scratch/probes-after.txt` prints `quoted marker commandLines []`, the suffix pair at count 2, `C exit=2 symlink_escape`, `E` with `trackedDotenv` and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines equal to before, and T005 to T014 passed the Opus verifier | Met | - |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/implementation-summary.md:74:| `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Modified | Shell write reader, anchored `COMMAND:` reader, suffix-free tally |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/implementation-summary.md:122:| Probes before and after | `sed -i`, `perl -pi`, `tee` and `cp` move from `kinds=shell unsafe=false` to `kinds=write unsafe=true`, the quoted marker from a start to `commandLines []`, the suffix pair from counts 1 and 1 to 2 and 2, arena cases A, B and C from exit 0 to `source_dirty`, `stale_build` and `symlink_escape`, and `match=agents_spawn` from `ok` to `hook-missing`. The `python write` line and the `remote-guard.mjs` lines stay as before (`scratch/probes-before.txt`, `scratch/probes-after.txt`) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:52:- A transcript scorer that reads `sed -i`, `perl -i`, `tee`, `cp`, `mv`, `rm`, `mkdir` and `touch` as writes, reads a `COMMAND:` line only where it opens its line outside a quote or a fence, and tallies a command with and without its mode suffix together.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:145:suffix pair commandLines [{\"seq\":0,\"command\":\"/deep:review\",\"state\":\"offered\",\"count\":1},{\"seq\":0,\"command\":\"/deep:review:auto\",\"state\":\"started\",\"count\":1}]\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:236:| `iter1-P2-mode-suffix-hides-repeat` | `commandLines` tallies the raw match (`:534-536`) | Tally on namespace and name through `commandParts` (D4, T005) |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:290:| `RAD/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Modify | Shell writes, the anchored `COMMAND:` line and the suffix tally |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/032-review-pass-five-remediation/spec.md:341:| REQ-005 | The eight othe