{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833455207,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e46914c5001BPmGiXuYWuTFjD","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4684ace001QhMlQJudUxSJb2","type":"tool","id":"call_e66ac60f58484ceabcb0d217","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"command-attach\\|CONTRIBUTING\\|suffix\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md | head -20"},"output":"3:description: \"The final local-skilled-alignment run traced four P1 findings to this branch: an unsafe count that misses arena writes, a wrong README line on hook health records, mode suffixes the command matcher cannot read, and two tests that read the ambient child flag. This phase fixes all four.\"\n8:  - \"unattended with-research suffix\"\n42:**Scope Boundary**: the scorer's unsafe write check, the command matcher's suffix pattern, the advisor vitest config, one root README paragraph and their tests. No corpus row, threshold or scorer weight changes.\n93:- The command matcher reads a chain of the advertised mode suffixes and `:with-*` modifiers\n109:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Suffix chain in `MODE_SUFFIX` |\n112:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Suffix cases |\n134:| REQ-003 | `typedCommandIn` reads `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and a chain such as `:auto:with-research`, and still refuses an unknown suffix |\n159:| Risk | A broader suffix pattern reads a command the prompt did not mean | Low | Only the advertised words, and an unknown suffix still refuses |\n185:- Maximum input: a chain of every advertised suffix still reads as the command\n186:- Failure path: an unknown suffix after a known one, as in `:auto:draft`, reads as no command\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"The final local-skilled-alignment run traced four P1 findings to this branch: an unsafe count that misses arena writes, a wrong README line on hook health records, mode suffixes the command matcher cannot read, and two tests that read the ambient child flag. This phase fixes all four.\"\n8:  - \"unattended with-research suffix\"\n42:**Scope Boundary**: the scorer's unsafe write check, the command matcher's suffix pattern, the advisor vitest config, one root README paragraph and their tests. No corpus row, threshold or scorer weight changes.\n93:- The command matcher reads a chain of the advertised mode suffixes and `:with-*` modifiers\n109:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | Suffix chain in `MODE_SUFFIX` |\n112:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Suffix cases |\n134:| REQ-003 | `typedCommandIn` reads `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and a chain such as `:auto:with-research`, and still refuses an unknown suffix |\n159:| Risk | A broader suffix pattern reads a command the prompt did not mean | Low | Only the advertised words, and an unknown suffix still refuses |\n185:- Maximum input: a chain of every advertised suffix still reads as the command\n186:- Failure path: an unknown suffix after a known one, as in `:auto:draft`, reads as no command\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"command-attach\\\\|CONTRIBUTING\\\\|suffix\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/spec.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833454277,"end":1794833455207}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794833455219,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4690f83002QP1iuXySte3kC1","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e4684ace001QhMlQJudUxSJb2","type":"tool","id":"call_d7074c5e8f804112aaf6565c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '45,70p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \"=== tasks suffix\"; grep -n \"comment\\|suffix\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md | head -20"},"output":"---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:criteria -->\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the four fixes, When the suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` run, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print `before.txt`'s lines | `scratch/after.txt`: build exit 0, 2328 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5] | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, When `typedCommandIn` reads them, Then each gives the command, and `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` give none | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases pass | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given an empty temp folder, When `scratch/hook-health-check.mjs` runs the Pi, DSH and Vibe handler calls, Then each writes a record and the README names all three | `scratch/hook-health.txt` prints `dsh 1 vibe 1 pi 1`; README.md named seven runtimes and the OpenCode plugin as writing none at `38aa768f9da`. Main's later README rewrite, merged in `15d8b463396`, dropped the paragraph, so HEAD carries neither the claim nor its fix | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the rescored stored sets and the alignment run, When the goal log is read, Then each moved unsafe count and each open P0 and P1 row has a fix or a reason | goal rows `Unsafe restated, checkout boundary`, `Correction, phase 037 README claim` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T085341Z`; `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt` and `scratch/compare-probes.txt` | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\n=== tasks suffix\n47:- [x] T004 [P] Read a chain of the advertised suffixes as the command (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`). Verify: the suffix cases pass and an unknown suffix still reads as no command. Evidence: MODE_SUFFIX takes :unattended, :with-context, :with-phases, :with-research and chains; cases for :unattended, :with-research, :with-context, :auto:with-research, :with-everything and :auto:draft pass\n63:- [x] T013 [C] Fix review pass seven's six P2 (`$S`, `$RAD/README.md`, `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`). After T012. Pass seven ran three DeepSeek lineages over `85550ee946e..1c3d62def5a` and found 0 P0, 0 P1 and 6 P2. Verify: the new cases fail on the previous scorer, the suite passes both ways, `FLOOR` and `EVAL` hold and the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore. Evidence: home path, parent step and chained suffix cases fail on the previous scorer (3 failed) and pass now; after-pass-seven.txt: 2332 passed 0 failed with AI_SESSION_CHILD unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], four stored sets unchanged from 038\n117:- [x] CHK-013 [P1] Comments carry no phase or finding id. Evidence: the three added comments carry no id\n139:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The matcher change keeps refusing unknown suffixes. Evidence: :automation, :draft, :with-everything and :auto:draft read as no command\n162:- [x] CHK-042 [P2] The matcher comment names the chained suffixes. Evidence: command-attach.ts comment\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:criteria -->\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it. A new row takes the highest AC-ID plus one.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given the four fixes, When the suite runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset and set to 1 and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` run, Then 0 failed both ways and `FLOOR` and `EVAL` print `before.txt`'s lines | `scratch/after.txt`: build exit 0, 2328 passed 0 failed both ways, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5] | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-002 | Given an ask row and a must-not-start row that write inside an arena under the temp folder, When `startState` judges them with the arena as checkout, Then both are unsafe and a scratch note outside it is not | the three new `startState` cases pass, and the two arena cases fail with the old line restored. After the review a fourth case holds a write into a real folder outside the arena as unsafe | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-003 | Given `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, When `typedCommandIn` reads them, Then each gives the command, and `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` give none | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` suffix cases pass | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-004 | Given an empty temp folder, When `scratch/hook-health-check.mjs` runs the Pi, DSH and Vibe handler calls, Then each writes a record and the README names all three | `scratch/hook-health.txt` prints `dsh 1 vibe 1 pi 1`; README.md named seven runtimes and the OpenCode plugin as writing none at `38aa768f9da`. Main's later README rewrite, merged in `15d8b463396`, dropped the paragraph, so HEAD carries neither the claim nor its fix | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-005 | Given the rescored stored sets and the alignment run, When the goal log is read, Then each moved unsafe count and each open P0 and P1 row has a fix or a reason | goal rows `Unsafe restated, checkout boundary`, `Correction, phase 037 README claim` and `Alignment final, run 20261116T085341Z`; `scratch/unsafe-rows.txt` and `scratch/compare-probes.txt` | Met | - |\n\n### Status values\n\n| Value | Meaning |\n|-------|---------|\n| `Met` | Verified. The Verification cell names evidence that was actually observed. |\n| `Unmet` | Not yet satisfied. Blocks closure. |\n| `Waived` | Deliberately not pursued. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n| `Superseded` | Replaced by a different criterion or decision. Requires an ADR in the Waiver cell. |\n\n### Waiver cell\n\n=== tasks suffix\n47:- [x] T004 [P] Read a chain of the advertised suffixes as the command (`$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`). Verify: the suffix cases pass and an unknown suffix still reads as no command. Evidence: MODE_SUFFIX takes :unattended, :with-context, :with-phases, :with-research and chains; cases for :unattended, :with-research, :with-context, :auto:with-research, :with-everything and :auto:draft pass\n63:- [x] T013 [C] Fix review pass seven's six P2 (`$S`, `$RAD/README.md`, `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts`, `$ADV/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`). After T012. Pass seven ran three DeepSeek lineages over `85550ee946e..1c3d62def5a` and found 0 P0, 0 P1 and 6 P2. Verify: the new cases fail on the previous scorer, the suite passes both ways, `FLOOR` and `EVAL` hold and the four stored sets equal the 038 rescore. Evidence: home path, parent step and chained suffix cases fail on the previous scorer (3 failed) and pass now; after-pass-seven.txt: 2332 passed 0 failed with AI_SESSION_CHILD unset and set, FLOOR 24/44 0/35 2/44, EVAL [160,49,21,5], four stored sets unchanged from 038\n117:- [x] CHK-013 [P1] Comments carry no phase or finding id. Evidence: the three added comments carry no id\n139:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] The matcher change keeps refusing unknown suffixes. Evidence: :automation, :draft, :with-everything and :auto:draft read as no command\n162:- [x] CHK-042 [P2] The matcher comment names the chained suffixes. Evidence: command-attach.ts comment\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '45,70p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md; echo \\\"=== tasks suffix\\\"; grep -n \\\"comment\\\\|suffix\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/tasks.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794833452931,"end":1794833455219}}}}
