{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794834269655,"sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","part":{"partID":"prt_1e47521ea001gKqMT72eJG3Gq4","sessionID":"ses_e1b9f9c05ffe74nsIz5B1nhkxa","messageID":"msg_1e474e5d90016tI449iJ7YBpiM","type":"tool","id":"call_703545338402417ab605bd2e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 004\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Lineage: `attach-docs-8` (fan-out child, session `fanout-attach-docs-8-1794832880917-x4m8iz`)\n- Area: `attach-docs` per `review/review-scope-8.txt`\n- Dimension: maintainability\n- Operator review focus: followed `review/review-brief-8.txt`. This iteration checks the reworded matcher comment against the suffix tests that are supposed to pin it, and the documentation quality of the changed `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence. The scorer area stays with `scorer-8`; no recorded limit is re-reported.\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (197-211 comment, 217-244 retired map and matcher) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (414-484) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442]\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md:155` [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md` (pass-seven plan seed, context evidence) [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md:121]\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **The rewritten comment defines a shared suffix rule that no suffix test pins, and the documented `:with-phases` modifier has no positive case** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442` -- The comment now says a `:with-*` modifier typed on a command that does not take it still names that command, and the constant reads `:with-phases`; the suffix suite types only modifiers each tested command advertises and never types `:with-phases`. Pass seven asked for that case in its plan seed, and the pass-seven fix commit (`3416b5e0526`) changed the comment without touching this test file.\n   - Finding class: `matrix/evidence` -- the test matrix does not cover a documented branch of the rule the comment states\n   - Scope proof: the suffix tests are the only guard for `MODE_SUFFIX`; a grep of `tests/` finds no `:with-phases` case and no `:with-*` case on a command that does not advertise it. The comment and the constant are in `command-attach.ts`; the plan seed is the prior remediation record.\n   - Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3`\n   - Case: a maintainer applies the other half of pass seven's own remediation choice and derives the suffix set per command from `argument-hint`. `phases` is dropped from the shared alternation, so `/speckit:plan:with-phases add a login page` -- a documented invocation at `plan.md:3` -- stops reading as `/speckit:plan`, while every suffix test stays green because `:with-phases` never appears in the file. The comment is the only record of the shared rule, so the regression has no failing check to catch it.\n\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3]\n\n   Why it is P2: the current matcher returns `/speckit:plan` for that input, so no user sees a wrong result today. The defect is the missing evidence row and the silent-regression path it leaves, not an active misread.\n\n   Fix recommendation: add one `it` case with `/speckit:plan:with-phases add a login page` (and optionally `/speckit:plan:with-research`, a modifier `plan.md` does not advertise) so the shared-rule sentence and the `phases` alternative both fail a suite when removed.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | pass | AC-003 pins `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, and the suite pins each of those plus the two refusal cases. The comment's shared-rule sentence and the `:with-phases` alternative are outside AC-003, which is why they are recorded as a matrix gap in the finding above rather than as an AC failure. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:56] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:435] |\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The target is a phase-parent packet with no `checklist.md`; the pass-eight brief and scope file are the operative checklist. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:1] |\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- The comment's rule and the constant are consistent: `/speckit:plan:with-research` names `/speckit:plan` even though `plan.md` does not advertise that modifier, and `/create:readme:with-research` names `/create:readme` for the same reason. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:205]\n- The pass-seven remediation record contains the exact test this pass still finds missing: \"Add a `:with-phases` case to `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` so the second advertised modifier is pinned.\" [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md:121]\n- The changed `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence is clear about the command's purpose and names the parent command for multi-mode skills; the wording adds no ambiguity. [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- A suffix followed by a file extension still reads as the command; the recorded limit stands and is not re-reported. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211]\n- The retired name typed in a question or refusal still attaches its successor; the packet records this as a phase 020 accepted limit (decision P045) and this iteration does not re-raise it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:242]\n- The comment's `:with-*` wildcard is narrower in code than the word suggests: only `context`, `phases` and `research` exist, and the hint sweep in iteration 2 found no fourth modifier. The shorthand does not mislead while the set matches the documents; the finding above is about the missing pin, not the shorthand.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The reworded comment no longer claims a per-command documentation rule; it states the shared union and names the chain example, which matches `MODE_SUFFIX`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\n- The suffix suite's positive and negative cases still pin every input AC-003 names, and the unknown-suffix cases keep `:automation`, `:draft`, `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` refused. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:448]\n- The `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence uses the live command name and the live parent command name, with no stale alias and no broken inline formatting. [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- The comment being inaccurate after the pass-seven rewrite: each sentence was reproduced against the matcher, including the shared-union sentence and the chain example.\n- A test that asserts the wrong command for a suffix input: each positive case names the command its hint advertises, and each negative case names an unknown suffix the matcher refuses.\n- A broken `CONTRIBUTING.md` command reference: iteration 2 resolved all six names under `.skilled/commands`.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: maintainability (stability pass over all four dimensions)\n- Focus area: re-read the finding's cited lines, confirm the dimension coverage record, and run one cross-reference pass before synthesis.\n- Reason: iteration 4 is the last first-coverage pass; the loop needs one stability pass so `coverageAge` reaches 1 before the fifth-iteration cap.\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions will be covered after this iteration; the stability pass follows.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the `:with-phases` matrix gap is the productive carry-forward; the deferred item is recorded in the report.\n- Required evidence: the finding's file:line and the pass-seven plan seed; no new code finding is expected.\n\nReview verdict: PASS\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Iteration 004\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Lineage: `attach-docs-8` (fan-out child, session `fanout-attach-docs-8-1794832880917-x4m8iz`)\\n- Area: `attach-docs` per `review/review-scope-8.txt`\\n- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Operator review focus: followed `review/review-brief-8.txt`. This iteration checks the reworded matcher comment against the suffix tests that are supposed to pin it, and the documentation quality of the changed `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence. The scorer area stays with `scorer-8`; no recorded limit is re-reported.\\n- Steer channel: `steer.md` does not exist in this lineage.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (197-211 comment, 217-244 retired map and matcher) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` (414-484) [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442]\\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md:155` [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md` (pass-seven plan seed, context evidence) [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md:121]\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **The rewritten comment defines a shared suffix rule that no suffix test pins, and the documented `:with-phases` modifier has no positive case** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442` -- The comment now says a `:with-*` modifier typed on a command that does not take it still names that command, and the constant reads `:with-phases`; the suffix suite types only modifiers each tested command advertises and never types `:with-phases`. Pass seven asked for that case in its plan seed, and the pass-seven fix commit (`3416b5e0526`) changed the comment without touching this test file.\\n   - Finding class: `matrix/evidence` -- the test matrix does not cover a documented branch of the rule the comment states\\n   - Scope proof: the suffix tests are the only guard for `MODE_SUFFIX`; a grep of `tests/` finds no `:with-phases` case and no `:with-*` case on a command that does not advertise it. The comment and the constant are in `command-attach.ts`; the plan seed is the prior remediation record.\\n   - Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3`\\n   - Case: a maintainer applies the other half of pass seven's own remediation choice and derives the suffix set per command from `argument-hint`. `phases` is dropped from the shared alternation, so `/speckit:plan:with-phases add a login page` -- a documented invocation at `plan.md:3` -- stops reading as `/speckit:plan`, while every suffix test stays green because `:with-phases` never appears in the file. The comment is the only record of the shared rule, so the regression has no failing check to catch it.\\n\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:442] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3]\\n\\n   Why it is P2: the current matcher returns `/speckit:plan` for that input, so no user sees a wrong result today. The defect is the missing evidence row and the silent-regression path it leaves, not an active misread.\\n\\n   Fix recommendation: add one `it` case with `/speckit:plan:with-phases add a login page` (and optionally `/speckit:plan:with-research`, a modifier `plan.md` does not advertise) so the shared-rule sentence and the `phases` alternative both fail a suite when removed.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | pass | AC-003 pins `:unattended`, `:with-research`, `:with-context` and `:auto:with-research`, and the suite pins each of those plus the two refusal cases. The comment's shared-rule sentence and the `:with-phases` alternative are outside AC-003, which is why they are recorded as a matrix gap in the finding above rather than as an AC failure. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/038-alignment-p1-remediation/acceptance-criteria.md:56] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:435] |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | The target is a phase-parent packet with no `checklist.md`; the pass-eight brief and scope file are the operative checklist. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:1] |\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- The comment's rule and the constant are consistent: `/speckit:plan:with-research` names `/speckit:plan` even though `plan.md` does not advertise that modifier, and `/create:readme:with-research` names `/create:readme` for the same reason. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:205]\\n- The pass-seven remediation record contains the exact test this pass still finds missing: \\\"Add a `:with-phases` case to `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` so the second advertised modifier is pinned.\\\" [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/review-report.md:121]\\n- The changed `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence is clear about the command's purpose and names the parent command for multi-mode skills; the wording adds no ambiguity. [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- A suffix followed by a file extension still reads as the command; the recorded limit stands and is not re-reported. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:211]\\n- The retired name typed in a question or refusal still attaches its successor; the packet records this as a phase 020 accepted limit (decision P045) and this iteration does not re-raise it. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md:242]\\n- The comment's `:with-*` wildcard is narrower in code than the word suggests: only `context`, `phases` and `research` exist, and the hint sweep in iteration 2 found no fourth modifier. The shorthand does not mislead while the set matches the documents; the finding above is about the missing pin, not the shorthand.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The reworded comment no longer claims a per-command documentation rule; it states the shared union and names the chain example, which matches `MODE_SUFFIX`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:203]\\n- The suffix suite's positive and negative cases still pin every input AC-003 names, and the unknown-suffix cases keep `:automation`, `:draft`, `:with-everything` and `:auto:draft` refused. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:448]\\n- The `CONTRIBUTING.md` sentence uses the live command name and the live parent command name, with no stale alias and no broken inline formatting. [SOURCE: CONTRIBUTING.md:155]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- The comment being inaccurate after the pass-seven rewrite: each sentence was reproduced against the matcher, including the shared-union sentence and the chain example.\\n- A test that asserts the wrong command for a suffix input: each positive case names the command its hint advertises, and each negative case names an unknown suffix the matcher refuses.\\n- A broken `CONTRIBUTING.md` command reference: iteration 2 resolved all six names under `.skilled/commands`.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: maintainability (stability pass over all four dimensions)\\n- Focus area: re-read the finding's cited lines, confirm the dimension coverage record, and run one cross-reference pass before synthesis.\\n- Reason: iteration 4 is the last first-coverage pass; the loop needs one stability pass so `coverageAge` reaches 1 before the fifth-iteration cap.\\n- Rotation status: all four dimensions will be covered after this iteration; the stability pass follows.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: the `:with-phases` matrix gap is the productive carry-forward; the deferred item is recorded in the report.\\n- Required evidence: the finding's file:line and the pass-seven plan seed; no new code finding is expected.\\n\\nReview verdict: PASS\\n\",\"path\":\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-docs-8/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794834244074,"end":1794834269655}}}}
